  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1233 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nModel agreement continues to see upper-level flow shift to a more\nnorthwesterly flow over the Panhandles as we get trapped between\ntwo closed upper-level low pressure systems. This flow is expected\nto keep us dry through Friday with chances of precipitation\ndropping below 10 percent. However, these drier conditions do open\nus to a little bit of warming with afternoon highs looking heat\nback into the 60s by Friday. Meanwhile, overnight lows look to\nstay chilly with most locations holding in the 30s. By Saturday,\nmodel agreement does have the upper-level flow shifting to a more\nzonal flow with the ECMWF trying to force another trough across\nthe Panhandles. However, most ensembles preferring to keeping\nconditions dry at this time with any chances of precipitation\nbelow 10 percent. Still, there may be some truth to this passage\nas latest ensemble runs have now come to an agreement on cooler\ntemperatures for Sunday with highs now expected to be in the 50s.\nEither way, temperature do look to warm right back up come Monday\nwith afternoon highs in the 60s once again.",
